e on the crisis  austria is leaning more towards the  german position to diplomacy they also  have very good relations with russia  economic deep economic relations with  russia while the eastern  eu member states are much more uh  wary are much more  aware of a russian threat and uh lean  more towards the western towards the  american position  now i i know materials that you've just  come back from eastern ukraine you're  there near areas controlled by  russian-backed separatists he visited a  village i understand right at the front  line let's take a look at your report  now  the village school of granite the last  village here on ukrainian controlled  territory is close to the front line it  has come under fire before  now the classrooms are empty not because  of the war but because of new covet  restrictions the war is something people  here have been living with for eight  years  we go to work and most of the time the  children go to school  but we don't know what will happen  in five or ten minutes  or tomorrow night  we're always worried always scared  just a few hundred meters down this road  is the last ukrainian position this  school is in the line of fire of the  opposite side  there is a heavy military presence in  granite  a ceasefire is in place but shelling can  sometimes  it was worse a few years ago we always  hid in the cellar when there was  fighting  but that was then  but with the latest russian buildup a  bigger escalation is on the table again  when things come down we bought a house  here  but now we don't know what will happen  ukrainian territory ends with the last  houses of the village  behind a small river lies a  demilitarized strip  the pedestrian bridge is the only link  to the next village in the so-called  gray zone  the next village is not small people  come here every day to work and kids go  to school  one of the people who crosses the border  every day is teacher ludmila kaczuk she  is from across the river and does not  want t